# Spotify Web API Guidelines

- **OpenAPI spec**: Use https://developer.spotify.com/reference/web-api/open-api-schema.yaml as the source of truth for endpoint paths, parameters, and response schemas. Do not guess endpoints or field names.
- **Authorization**:
  - User-specific data: Authorization Code with PKCE ([docs](https://developer.spotify.com/documentation/web-api/tutorials/code-pkce-flow)).
  - With a secure backend, Authorization Code ([docs](https://developer.spotify.com/documentation/web-api/tutorials/code-flow)) is also acceptable.
  - Client Credentials only for public, non-user data.
  - Never use the Implicit Grant flow (deprecated).
- **Redirect URIs** ([docs](https://developer.spotify.com/documentation/web-api/concepts/redirect_uri)): Always HTTPS, except `http://127.0.0.1` for local development. Never use `http://localhost` or wildcard URIs.
- **Scopes** ([docs](https://developer.spotify.com/documentation/web-api/concepts/scopes)): Request only the minimum scopes needed for the feature being built. Never request broad scopes preemptively.
- **Token management** ([refresh docs](https://developer.spotify.com/documentation/web-api/tutorials/refreshing-tokens)):
  - Store tokens securely.
  - Never expose the Client Secret in client-side code.
  - Implement token refresh; send the user through authorization again when the refresh token expires.
- **Rate limits**: On HTTP 429, use exponential backoff and respect the `Retry-After` header. Never retry immediately or in tight loops.
- **Deprecated endpoints**: Do not use them.
  - Prefer `/playlists/{id}/items` over `/playlists/{id}/tracks`.
  - Prefer `/me/library` over the type-specific library endpoints.
- **Error handling**: Handle every HTTP error code documented in the OpenAPI schema. Read the returned error message and surface meaningful feedback to the user.
- **Developer Terms** ([terms](https://developer.spotify.com/terms)):
  - Do not cache Spotify content beyond what is needed for immediate use.
  - Always attribute content to Spotify.
  - Never use Spotify data to train machine learning models.
